@moazzamak/dsh-code-review README · @moazzamak/dsh-code-review：A code-review pack for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (`dsh`). It adds a `/review` command that opens the newest turn's changed files, compared one by one, and a Skill that tells the agent what that record covers and how to keep a turn cheap to review.

> **Unofficial community pack.** Not affiliated with, endorsed by, or published by DeepSeek. See [Naming and affiliation](#naming-and-affiliation).

English | [中文](README.zh.md)

@moazzamak/dsh-code-review README · What you get：- **`/review`** — opens the newest recorded turn's changed files in the right sidebar. Each row is one file; opening it shows that file's turn-start and turn-end contents as hunks, side by side or unified, with line wrapping. `/review` appears only while all three of these hold: the comparison view is registered, the Session's right column is mounted, and the Session has a turn whose changes were recorded. A command whose page has nowhere to open is worse than an absent command, so the pack hides it rather than offering a no-op.
- **The `dsh-change-review` Skill** — what the agent cannot learn from a tool result: that a turn, not a tool call, is the unit you review; that only top-level turns are recorded, so a subagent's edits are never in your diff; that a Session reopened after a Host restart has no comparison for its earlier turns; and that nothing is reverted, so a comment on a change means the change is still in the file.
- **Precedence over the built-in diff card** — while the pack is installed, dsh's own changed-files card no longer appears under each turn, so `/review` is the way into a turn's changes rather than one of two.

